course: dictionary
lesson: 1751
title: Classmate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A classmate is a person in the same class as you at school. The word has two parts: class, a group learning together, and mate, a friend. So a classmate is someone you learn with every day.
explain: The lesson tells you more: «be kind to a new classmate» shows a classmate is a person you treat well. «Tell a teacher if a classmate is hurt» shows a classmate can feel hurt, so a classmate is a child, never a thing.
explain: Classmates are people, so one classmate is one person and several are classmates. Try the swap check: put "a person in my class" in place of "classmate" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A classmate is a person in the same class as you at school.
fact: Classmate is a noun. Its plural is «classmates».
fact: Class means a group learning together, and mate means a friend.
fact: Classmates are people, so treat them with kindness and respect.
fact: Some classmates have health conditions, and none of these is catching or anyone's fault.
exercise: «Be kind to a new classmate.» What is a classmate? | A school building | *A person in the same class as you at school | A lesson in maths | A teacher who runs the class
exercise: Six classmates share 12 stickers equally. How many stickers does each classmate get? | *2 | 18 | 12 | 6
exercise: Which word is the plural of classmate? | *classmates | classmate | classmat | classmen
test: «Tell a teacher if a classmate is hurt.» What should you do if a classmate is hurt? | Ignore it | Laugh about it | *Tell a teacher | Hide it from everyone
test: Which sentence uses classmate correctly? | Classmate is a bright colour | The dog is my classmate | *My classmates and I work in pairs at school | The classmate was a shop on the corner
exam: A classmate's family is private, so what should you do with what you heard about it? | *Do not pass it on | Share it with everyone | Tell the whole class at break | Write it on the board
